{"Missing key prop on GrafanaRuleListItem. The key variable is destructured from ruleWithOrigin and used by the other two cases in this switch, but was dropped when replacing GrafanaRuleLoader. Without it, React cannot efficiently reconcile list items.": 0.9831866025924683, "\"Silence notifications\" menu action is non-functional for Grafana rules in filter view. GrafanaRuleListItem passes only promRule to RuleActionsButtons, but the silence drawer is gated on rulerRuleType.grafana.alertingRule(rule) where rule (the ruler DTO) is undefined. The menu item appears but clicking it does nothing because the drawer's render condition is never satisfied.": 0.8635089993476868, "ui.menuItems.delete selector is defined but never used in any test. Either the test for \"correct menu actions\" is missing an assertion for the delete action (the count should be 5 instead of 4, since AlertingRuleDelete is granted), or the selector is dead code and should be removed.": 0.649295449256897, "The imported groupIdentifier utility is shadowed by the groupIdentifier parameter in useAllRulerRuleAbilities, useRulerRuleAbility, and useRulerRuleAbilities. Consider renaming the import or the parameters to avoid shadowing.": 0.1790294647216797, "canDelete can now be true from grafana prom abilities without rulerRule, but the delete menu item's render condition still guards on rulerRule &&, and handleDelete requires rulerRule as an argument. In the list view without ruler, the grafana delete ability makes canDelete true but the delete option never renders.": 0.8016229271888733, "canPause can now be true from grafana prom abilities without rulerRule, but the pause menu item's render condition still requires rulerRuleType.grafana.rule(rulerRule). When rulerRule is absent, the pause item never renders, yet canPause still feeds into the showDivider calculation, which can produce a stray divider with no items above it.": 0.6996676921844482, "useGrafanaPromRuleAbility (singular) is imported, mocked, and configured but no component in the RulesTable tree calls it. This is dead test setup that also creates an inconsistency: it's explicitly configured in the first Grafana test but not the other three.": 0.4631371796131134, "Unnecessary optional chaining on rule?.health, rule?.lastError, and rule?.isPaused. rule is a required prop and is already destructured above, so it cannot be nullish here. The optional chaining is misleading about the nullability contract.": 0.30747538805007935, "Leftover // duplicate comment should be removed. It reads like a development note rather than meaningful documentation, and will confuse maintainers.": 0.5872536897659302}